  "decisions": [
    "fired-mould uses ward_grow (8% HP) and timed block (+20 for 3 s) without taking the stance slot so it coexists cleanly with mountain-stance (clay-mould-primer L2)",
    "ward-peal applies its 2.0 s next-art delay to any foe in duels because neither engine has a foe.creature readable, keeping creature-fleeing in lore and rule text",
    "carriage-bell, hang-the-bells, Rings as It Moves, and Forty Answer check own.foe_pressed >= 1 or foe.since_act <= 1 (with time > 1) on pulse so foes with exact-integer cooldowns trigger reliably in both engines",
    "pulse-driven bell tolls (carriage-bell, the-bell-that-rings-itself, Forty Answer) use one-shot summon (cd 0.5, for 0.6) while item/set free_hit rings use outside_budget: true to avoid pulse trig_budget clipping",
    "struck-it-answers returns 35% Physical damage on both was_hit and ward_absorbed (laying 1 Metal stack on was_hit only) with cooldown 8 s so ward-heavy builds return the full blow and fire even in short --gap 1 fights",
    "hang-the-bells gates its free foreseen-fight start on tag.foreseen >= 1, which compiles cleanly in both engines and activates automatically once foreseen is added to REQUEST_TAGS",
    "set rarity: 5 on ml-luan-bell (kind treasure, grade 4) to satisfy lint_items.py without changing modifiers"
  ],
